WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
EPA 608 is not optional. You cannot legally touch refrigerant without it. Let's
make sure you pass.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:40.000
A2L refrigerants are the future of the HVAC industry. The AIM Act (American
Innovation and Manufacturing Act) is phasing down HFCs including R-410A.
Replacements include R-454B (Opteon XL41, GWP 466), R-32 (GWP 675), and R-466A

00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:20.000
AIM Act: American Innovation and Manufacturing Act. Phases down HFC production
and use in the US.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:40.000
R-454B: Primary A2L replacement for R-410A in new residential systems. Trade
name Opteon XL41. GWP 466.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:00.000
GWP: Global Warming Potential. Measured relative to CO2 (GWP=1). R-410A
GWP=2,088. R-454B GWP=466.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Here's why this matters on the job: New residential systems are already shipping
with R-454B. If you are not trained on A2L handling you will not be able to
service new equipment within 2-3 years.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Watch out for these: Never use R-410A tools on A2L systems without verifying A2L
rating. And — A2L does not mean safe to ignore — it still requires proper
ventilation

00:02:40.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Quick check: what is the maximum fine for knowingly venting refrigerant? If you
don't know that number, go back and read it again.

